cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "amr-archetypes: recurring resistance profiles in a bacterial collection, and the diagnostics that decide whether they are real"
abstract: >-
  Clusters one or more binary genotype layers of a bacterial collection
  (acquired antimicrobial-resistance determinants, virulence loci, capsule or
  antigen type, plasmid replicons) by similarity-network fusion with
  order-invariant neighbour selection and consensus clustering, selects a
  number of groups that may be one, and reports the diagnostics that decide
  whether the resulting partition means anything: whether the largest group
  is the trait-absent stratum produced by the empty-union distance convention,
  whether tied affinities make the answer depend on input row order, whether
  the fusion collapsed onto a single layer, whether co-inherited loci inflate
  the feature count, and whether the groups are the lineages relabelled, the
  last measured as the lineage-attributable share of the partition by the
  out-of-sample variance decomposition of amr-clonalshare, on which the
  package depends. Post-clustering inference uses multi-split feature
  splitting with a p-value merging rule valid for exchangeable, arbitrarily
  dependent p-values, and separates "there is structure" from "that structure
  is discrete" with a parametric bootstrap from a BIC-selected latent-trait
  continuum model with adaptive dimension checking and exact finite-bootstrap
  uncertainty; an exact, closed-form phylogenetic convergence test serves
  small cohorts. Every candidate partition, the fusion, the naive
  concatenation, each single layer and a Bernoulli mixture, is put through
  the same held-out test, and a measured phenotype, where one is supplied, is
  the one criterion that is not a function of what was clustered. A
  five-level machine-readable claim ladder exposes every applicable gate and
  prevents a partition from being promoted directly to a biological
  archetype; a failed gate closes the run with a non-zero exit code. Ships
  two independently seeded positive controls, negative and adversarial
  controls, and documented Klebsiella pneumoniae and Streptococcus suis case
  studies in which statistical discreteness and biological interpretation
  are reported separately.
type: software
